  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_brigid",
      "name": {
        "en": "Brigid's Badge",
        "zh": "水灯心证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_brigid",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Brigid has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for repeatedly attacking approaching enemies with a boomerang projectile.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Loopshooter responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员水灯心擅长操纵回旋投射物往复打击靠近的敌人\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使回环射手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_brigid",
      "name": {
        "en": "Color of the Wind",
        "zh": "风的颜色",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_brigid",
      "description": {
        "en": "Brigid tries to pick up the tent toppled by wind, but finds that as soon as she tries to pick up one side, the other side falls over. Her hair is wet from the rain, which flows along her forehead and into her eyes. She fidgets at the uncomfortable sensation of her clothes being stuck to her skin. They are getting heavier, and colder. 'It's no good', she mutters, as she reluctantly lays down the canvas and sticks.\nBrigid spreads open a map made from beast hide, running her finger over it to find the nearest shelter—a Catastrophe Messenger hut about two kilometers from her location, in the same direction as the wind. Perhaps she can make it if she runs? Fortunately, the burdenbeasts have been housed, and she only needs find a place for herself tonight.\n'Run, Brigid, run. You can keep running if you do not find the hut, until you reach the town, or perhaps a little shed along the way that would provide shelter against the rain.' Then, she sees the faint silhouette of a house in the distance. She wipes the raindrops off her face and takes cover under the eaves. She knocks on the door, but there is no answer. There're knots signifying 'safety' hanging from the doors and windows. She touches them before going in.\nNo one has been here for a while. Even the knots at the door have grown hardened and pricked her hands. At least the roof is in good shape, keeping the wind and rain out. Brigid lays down her luggage, finds some wood to light a fire, and hangs a rope to dry her clothes. Finally, she puts all the dried fabric she can find in a bundle before the fireplace and huddles up with her hair still wet, slumbering away while the rain continues battering the windows.\nThe fire has gone out by the time she wakes up, but she feels no cold. She frees herself from the bundle of cloth and walks towards the windows. She notices that the knots she saw yesterday have been all blown away, some falling into the mud, and others flying quite a distance, hanging on the trees.\nBefore she leaves, she takes out some ropes from her luggage and ties two knots in the same fashion as the ones she found, hanging one at the door and the other at the windows.\n'Thanks for the hospitality!'\nIt is bright and sunny outside. Looking back, she realizes that the hut is quite old and battered. She thanks the hut and looks up at the sky.\n'Thank you wind, thank you rain, for taking it easy—'\nA breeze sways the knots hanging in front of the windows, causing the chimes upon them to ring, perhaps in response, or perhaps in farewell.",
        "zh": "布莉吉试着把被吹得东歪西倒的帐篷从地上扶起来，发现只要用手拽起一边，另一边就会倒下去。雨水渐密，已经把她的头发打湿，顺着前额流进眼睛。她不舒服地动了动身体，感觉衣服也越来越重，黏在皮肤上，冻得人直摇头。不行了，没用。她嘟囔着，依依不舍地放下手里的帐篷布，还有用来代替伸缩杆的木棍。\n布莉吉把刻着地图的兽皮摊开，手指在上面摩挲，找到了离这里最近的那个凹点。有个天灾信使小屋，距离这里……两公里！顺风方向，跑快一点，也许可以？还好驮兽们都已经提前安置了，现在只需要给自己找个地方过夜。\n跑吧，跑吧。如果找不到，那就再跑几公里，去镇上看看，有个能遮雨的棚子也好。这样想着，房屋模糊的形状逐渐在视野里出现。游牧人甩掉脸上的雨珠，冲到屋檐下。敲门，没人响应，她看到门窗上都挂着喻示“安全”的绳结，伸出手去摸了摸，才推门进去。\n看起来这里已经很久没有人维护，就连门口的绳结也硬得扎手，但至少屋顶还好好的，雨水下不来，大风刮不进。布莉吉放下行李，在屋子里找到干柴生火，又牵起一条绳子用来烤干换下来的衣服。最后，把能找到的干燥布料都堆在壁炉前，布莉吉躺进去蜷缩起来，也不管头发还湿着，就在噼啪的雨声中沉沉睡去。\n醒来时，壁炉里的火早已熄灭，但布莉吉没有感觉到寒冷。她从绞作一团的布料中挣脱出来，走到窗户前，注意到昨天来时在门窗上看到的绳结都已经被吹落了。它们有的掉在泥地里，有的飘出去很远，挂在了树梢上。\n临走之前，布莉吉从行李里取出材料，照着捡回来的绳结的样式，编起了新的绳结。她编了两个，一个挂在门上，一个挂在窗上。\n“谢谢收留！”\n屋外，天光大亮，晴日已经悬在头顶。昨天来时没有细看，眼前的房屋其实已经有些年头，几乎可以说是摇摇欲坠，布莉吉对房子道了谢，又转头望向天空。\n“也谢谢风，谢谢雨，谢谢你们‘手下留情’——”\n身后，风再度吹起挂在窗前的绳结，上面绑着的铃铛叮铃作响，像是回应，也像是告别。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
